id: ops-kw02
title: Make historical Windows proof evidence available in fresh clones
description: "After merging reviewed repair PR #150 with main, CI run 38116691747 fails on Linux and Windows because test/windows-proof-history.test.ts loads test/windows-consumers.proof.ts from b89fd6f36adf91c9bfc784c7ab643d9ce9cb7eae, a development commit outside branch ancestry. The canonical object cache masks this failure. A fresh single-branch clone of #150 reproduces it. Preserve strict historical source-only proof refusal while replacing unavailable development-history dependencies with portable, provenance-linked evidence. This follow-up does not change reviewed repair behavior."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-11T06:12:11.492Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T23:29:08.647Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-11T23:29:08.624Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-11T23:29:08.624Z"
author: codex-agent
parent: ops-hiee
repro_steps: "Clone the feature branch into a fresh repository and run node --test test/windows-proof-history.test.ts; git show b89fd6f36adf91c9bfc784c7ab643d9ce9cb7eae:test/windows-consumers.proof.ts fails."
resolution: "Implemented and merged in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/156: historical Windows proof fixtures are vendored so fresh clones no longer need orphaned commits"
expected_result: The acceptance criteria recorded on ops-kw02 are met on main.
actual_result: "Merged in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/156 after its full CI, an isolated release gate and a CodeRabbit full review with every finding resolved; historical Windows proof fixtures are vendored so fresh clones no longer need orphaned commits"
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-11T08:16:31.940Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed root cause in CI run 38117928292 and a fresh single-branch clone: 1 test, 0 passed, 1 failed while loading b89fd6f proof source. Both checkout jobs already use fetch-depth: 0. Main 3fca1f2 has the same test; passing run 38122425892 includes c69400b, which independently replaces historical controls with frozen function strings. The feature merge did not introduce a separate checkout or test difference. Vendoring the complete pre-diagnostic proof preserves the explicit missing-history refusal test. Frozen old launcher functions preserve current consumer assertions; the availability guard names reachable main squash commit 3fca1f2. Preparing the same focused change in a separate main PR."
  "2026-10-11T08:16:57.359Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replacing only replaceFunction with a no-op while retaining the new tests yields 2 tests, 1 pass, 1 failure. Removing only the explicit missing-history assertion from the native proof yields 2 tests, 1 pass, 1 failure. Both changes were restored; node --test test/windows-proof-history.test.ts and pm test ops-kw02 --run --progress each pass 2/2 with zero failures or skips. Linked result tracking is disabled by existing configuration, so this comment records the receipt."
  "2026-10-11T08:18:17.988Z",codex-agent,"The separate fix/vendor-historical-proof-fixture branch starts at origin/main 3fca1f2 and contains only durable Windows proof fixtures, function controls, regression coverage and this existing tracker item. Reusing ops-kw02 from the feature branch avoids a duplicate issue. The same two function/diagnostic behavioral revert checks apply; focused regression passes 2/2. Main has the same deleted-branch dependency and needs this fix independently of PR #150."
  "2026-10-11T08:48:06.472Z",codex-agent,"Final main-branch receipts: npm run release:check, bun run release:check, and env HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check all pass under Node 22. Every suite reports 579 tests, 577 passed, 0 failed, 2 pre-existing optional fleet-data skips, 0 canceled/TODO; all 23 configured source files report 100/100/100/100. Type checking, lint, 0% duplication, documentation, production audit, packing, changelog and release-policy checks pass without threshold or timeout changes. CI run 38124425559 at 83cc5c0 passes Linux and native Windows Node 22/26; native logs reject both function reverts and actual npm 10.9.4 before packing. Main-local function-only no-op and diagnostic-only behavioral reverts each fail one of two regressions; restored focused and PM-linked runs pass 2/2. PR #156 is the independent focused fix from main. Result tracking is disabled by existing PM configuration; receipts are preserved here. No new PM CLI/SDK defect was found. Leaving the item in_progress and releasing the claim for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-11T11:20:01.156Z",codex-agent,"Final feature-branch receipts: npm run release:check (Node 24), bun run release:check (Node 22 on PATH), and env HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check (Node 22) all pass. Each suite reports 598 tests, 596 passed, 0 failed, 2 pre-existing optional fleet-data skips, 0 canceled/TODO; all 25 configured source files report 100/100/100/100. CI run 38124385545 passes Linux Node 22/26 and native Windows Node 22/26. Windows logs explicitly reject both source-only function reverts and actual npm 10.9.4 before packing. Both regression behavioral reverts fail 1/2 as expected; restored focused and PM-linked regressions pass 2/2. Separate main PR #156 also passes all four CI jobs. Result recording remains disabled by existing PM configuration; these comments preserve receipts. No new PM CLI/SDK defect was found."
